# Offline editor journey. No Start Map, provider calls, or scan dispatch.
name: Budget editing discloses retrospective stops and preserves explicit choices
size: 40x12
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 READY THE MAP RUN | setup
keys: Down Down Down Down Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 SESSION BUDGET | budget-editor
expect: Observed spend stop
expect: overspend
expect: Enter save
expect: Esc cancel
type: -5
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Amount must be finite | invalid-amount
expect: -5
expect: Enter save
expect: Esc cancel
ask: Are the draft, rejection, spending limitation and save/cancel controls readable in this narrow terminal?
keys: C-u
type: 2.50
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 OBSERVED STOP | saved-stop
expect-not: Budget ENFORCED
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 SESSION BUDGET | reopen-saved
expect: $2.5
keys: C-u
type: 99
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 OBSERVED STOP | cancel-edit
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 SESSION BUDGET | saved-choice-preserved
expect: $2.5
expect-not: $99
ask: Is the prior setting preserved after cancellation, with no claim of a guaranteed dollar ceiling or newly launched work?
keys: C-c
